## Credentials

All passwords are in `.env.local` (mode 0600, git-ignored). Keep that file private.
{{- if .Secure }}
Docker Compose reads it as the source of its secrets. Containers get each secret as a
file in `/run/secrets`, never as an environment variable, so `docker inspect` does not show them.
{{- end }}

| Service | User | Password in `.env.local` |
| --- | --- | --- |
{{- if .Config.DefaultUsers }}
| OpenArch | `admin`, `testuser` and the other users bundled in the image | none: all use `password` |
{{- else }}
| OpenArch | `{{ .AdminUser }}` | `OPENARCH_ADMIN_PASSWORD` |
{{- end }}
{{- if .Secure }}
| MongoDB (root) | `{{ .MongoRootUser }}` | `MONGODB_ROOT_PASSWORD` |
| MongoDB (OpenArch, database `{{ .MongoAppDB }}`) | `{{ .MongoAppUser }}` | `MONGODB_APP_PASSWORD` |
| OpenSearch (admin) | `{{ .OpenSearchAdminUser }}` | `OPENSEARCH_ADMIN_PASSWORD` |
| OpenSearch (OpenArch) | `{{ .OpenSearchAppUser }}` | `OPENSEARCH_APP_PASSWORD` |
{{- if .Config.Has "dashboards" }}
| OpenSearch Dashboards (server) | `{{ .DashboardsUser }}` | `OPENSEARCH_DASHBOARDS_PASSWORD` |
{{- end }}

`config/users.yml` and `config/opensearch/internal_users.yml` hold only bcrypt hashes.
After a change of the OpenArch admin password or the MongoDB OpenArch password, run
`openarch render`, then `openarch up`.
The MongoDB root password and the OpenSearch passwords apply only when the data is created.
OpenSearch serves plain HTTP inside the Docker network, with users and passwords required.
{{- else }}

`insecureBackends` is on: MongoDB and OpenSearch have no authentication.
{{- end }}
{{- if eq .Config.TLS.Mode "self-signed" }}

## TLS

The certificate in `certs/` is self-signed, so browsers and clients do not trust it by default.
It is valid for {{ .Config.ServerName }}, localhost and 127.0.0.1.
{{- else if eq .Config.TLS.Mode "custom" }}

## TLS

The proxy uses the certificate `{{ .Config.TLS.Cert }}` and the key `{{ .Config.TLS.Key }}`.
{{- end }}

## Storage

{{ if .Volume -}}
Data is kept in Docker named volumes: `{{ .Config.Name }}_mongodb-data`, `{{ .Config.Name }}_opensearch-data` and `{{ .Config.Name }}_openarch-data`.
`docker compose down` keeps them. `docker compose down -v` deletes them.
{{- else if .Bind -}}
Data is kept in `{{ .DataDir }}`: one folder each for MongoDB, OpenSearch and OpenArch files.
{{- else -}}
Storage is `none`: no data is kept when the containers are removed.
{{- end }}

## Run

```
openarch up
openarch status
openarch logs openarch-app -f
openarch down
```

## Run without the CLI

```
docker compose --env-file .env --env-file .env.local up -d
docker compose ps
docker compose logs -f openarch-app
docker compose down
```
